# Both Dockerfiles take the repository root as their build context — the server image needs src/ and
# pepperx.json, the dashboard image needs dashboard/ and docker/dashboard/nginx.conf. That makes this
# file worth keeping tight: the whole context is uploaded to the Docker Build Cloud builder on every
# build, so excluding what the images never read is the difference between a fast build and a slow one.

# Build output
**/bin/
**/obj/
**/dist/
**/artifacts/
**/TestResults/
**/test-artifacts/
**/.vs/
**/.vite/
**/.idea/
**/*.user

# Dependencies — restored inside the image, never copied in
**/node_modules/

# Python SDK artifacts
**/__pycache__/
**/*.egg-info/
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
**/.mypy_cache/
**/.venv/

# Runtime state
data/
logs/
*.log
results.json
perf-baseline.json

# Not read by either image
.git/
.github/
.gitignore
.dockerignore
sdk/
postman/
memory/
assets/
dashboard/qa/
dashboard/qa-output*/
*.md
*.bat
